<html>
<title>HEX and XMODEM Support</title>
<body>


<h1>HEX and XMODEM Support</h1>

<p>
HEX or XMODEM file transfer will be activated if the selected XML file includes a HEX or XMODEM definition.
</p>


<h2>HEX Support</h2>

<p>
The main controls for HEX Support are shown in the screenshot below. The numbered markers in the screenshot correspond to the descriptions in this section.
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/computer_hexmodem.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>
<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>HEX</strong> button</li>
<li>(2) <strong>HEX</strong> text field (selected file)</li>
<li>(3) <strong>Eject</strong> button</li>
<li>(4) <strong>Auto</strong> checkbox</li>
<li>(5) <strong>Turbo</strong> checkbox</li>
<li>(6) <strong>Play</strong> button</li>
<li>(7) <strong>Stop</strong> button</li>
<li>(8) <strong>Record</strong> button</li>
<li>(9) <strong>CPU speed</strong> field (MHz)</li>
</ul>

<p>
A HEX file can be loaded in configurations such as Elf 2000 (when using a terminal), CDP18S020 Evaluation Kit Emulator, Membership Card and VIP2K Membership Card.
</p>

<p>
Press the <strong>HEX</strong> button (1) and select a file.<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> The selected file is shown in the HEX text field (2).
</p>

<p>
Press the <strong>Eject</strong> button (3).<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> The selected file is cleared.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> The default and simplest method is <strong>Auto file transfer</strong> (4). For faster transfer, select the <strong>Turbo</strong> checkbox (5).
</p>


<h3>Workflow</h3>

<pre>
Select File     : Press the HEX button
Start Transfer  : Auto file transfer or press the Play or Record button
Stop Transfer   : Press the Stop button
Turbo Mode      : Enable for faster transfer
</pre>


<h3>Elf 2000 (Manual only)</h3>

<p>
Clear the <strong>Auto</strong> checkbox (4).
</p>

<p>
Start an Elf 2000 emulator<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> The Elf 2000 monitor starts and shows the <tt>>>></tt> prompt.
</p>


<h4>Loading</h4>

<p>
Press the <strong>Play</strong> button (6).<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> HEX data is shown on the terminal window.
</p>

<p>
When the last line shows <tt>>>>:00000001FF</tt>, press <tt>RETURN</tt>; <tt>EOF</tt> is shown, indicating end of file.
</p>

<p>
Press the <strong>Stop</strong> button (7) to stop the transfer.
</p>


<h3>CDP18S020 Evaluation Kit (Manual only)</h3>

<p>
Clear the <strong>Auto</strong> checkbox (4).
</p>

<p>
Start a CDP18S020 Evaluation Kit emulator<br>
Press <tt>RETURN</tt><br>
<strong>Result:</strong> The UT4 monitor starts and shows the <tt>*</tt> prompt.
</p>


<h4>Loading</h4>

<p>
<strong>Command:</strong> Type <tt>!M</tt>.
</p>

<p>
Press the <strong>Play</strong> button (6).<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> Unreadable data is shown on the terminal window.
</p>

<p>
Press the <strong>Stop</strong> button (7), when terminal output stops, to stop the transfer.
</p>


<h4>Saving</h4>

<p>
<strong>Command:</strong> Type <tt>?M&lt;start&gt; &lt;length&gt;</tt>.
</p>

<p>
Press the <strong>Record</strong> button (8) and then press <tt>RETURN</tt>.<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> Output data is shown on the terminal window.
</p>

<p>
Press the <strong>Stop</strong> button (7), when terminal output stops, to stop the transfer.
</p>


<h3>Membership Card and VIP2K Membership Card</h3>

<p>
The following describes HEX file transfer for the Membership Card and VIP2K Membership Card using the monitor software.
</p>

<p>
Start a Membership Card emulator<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> The Membership Card monitor starts and shows the <tt>></tt> prompt.
</p>


<h4>Auto LOAD/SAVE</h4>

<p>
<strong>Command:</strong> Press <tt>L</tt> to load a program or <tt>I</tt> to load a Chip-8 program.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Command:</strong> Press <tt>S</tt> to save.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> For the Membership Card: when save is finished the front panel LEDs flash; press a key in the terminal window.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> Make sure a file is selected (2). Otherwise, the emulator may hang or no file will be written.
</p>


<h4>Manual LOAD/SAVE</h4>

<p>
Clear the <strong>Auto</strong> checkbox (4).
</p>


<h5>Loading</h5>

<p>
<strong>Command:</strong> Press <tt>L</tt> to load a program or <tt>I</tt> to load a Chip-8 program.<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> Terminal shows <tt>Ready to LOAD Program</tt>.
</p>

<p>
Press the <strong>Play</strong> button (6).<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> The selected file is loaded.
</p>


<h5>Saving</h5>

<p>
<strong>Command:</strong> Press <tt>S</tt> to save.<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> Terminal shows <tt>Ready to SAVE Program</tt>.
</p>

<p>
Press the <strong>Record</strong> button (8).<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> The selected file is saved.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> For the Membership Card: when save is finished the front panel LEDs flash; press a key in the terminal window.
</p>


<h3>Turbo file transfer</h3>

<p>
Select the <strong>Turbo</strong> checkbox (5).<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> Emulator CPU speed is increased during file transfer.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> Default speed is 15 MHz (9); higher values may be used on faster systems.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Important:</strong> Too high values may cause performance issues on slower systems.
</p>


<h2>XMODEM Support</h2>

<p>
The main controls for XMODEM Support are shown in the screenshot below. The numbered markers in the screenshot correspond to the descriptions in this section.
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/computer_xmodem.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>
<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>XMODEM</strong> button</li>
<li>(2) <strong>XMODEM</strong> text field (selected file)</li>
<li>(3) <strong>Eject</strong> button</li>
<li>(4) <strong>Auto</strong> checkbox</li>
<li>(5) <strong>Turbo</strong> checkbox</li>
<li>(6) <strong>Play</strong> button</li>
<li>(7) <strong>Stop</strong> button</li>
<li>(8) <strong>Record</strong> button</li>
<li>(9) <strong>VT Setup</strong> button</li>
</ul>

<p>
Press the <strong>XMODEM</strong> button (1) and select a file.<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> The selected file is shown in the XMODEM text field (2).
</p>

<p>
Press the <strong>Eject</strong> button (3).<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> The selected file is cleared.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> The default and simplest method is <strong>Auto file transfer</strong> (4). For faster transfer, select the <strong>Turbo</strong> checkbox (5).
</p>


<h3>Workflow</h3>

<pre>
Select File     : Press the XMODEM button
Start Transfer  : Use xr/xs/yr/ys commands
Manual Mode     : Use Play / Record buttons
Stop Transfer   : Press the Stop button
</pre>


<h3>Auto file transfer</h3>

<p>
Select the <strong>Auto</strong> checkbox (4).
</p>

<p>
<strong>Command:</strong> Type <tt>xr</tt>, <tt>xrb</tt>, <tt>xs</tt>, <tt>xsb</tt>, <tt>yr</tt> or <tt>ys</tt> in Elf/Os.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> For <tt>xr</tt>, <tt>xrb</tt>, <tt>xs</tt>, <tt>xsb</tt>, only one file is used.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> The <tt>yr</tt> command supports multiple files.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> The <tt>ys</tt> command uses filenames defined in Elf/Os.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> If no file is selected, Elf/Os will wait. Clear the <strong>Auto</strong> checkbox (4) and use manual transfer.
</p>


<h3>Manual file transfer</h3>

<p>
Clear the <strong>Auto</strong> checkbox (4).
</p>

<p>
<strong>Command:</strong> Start the file transfer command in Elf/Os.
</p>

<p>
Press the <strong>Play</strong> button (6) to send to Elf/Os.<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> The selected file is loaded.
</p>

<p>
Press the <strong>Record</strong> button (8) to receive from Elf/Os.<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> The selected file is saved.
</p>

<p>
Press the <strong>Stop</strong> button (7) to stop the transfer.
</p>


<h3>Turbo file transfer</h3>

<p>
Select the <strong>Turbo</strong> checkbox (5).<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> Emulator CPU speed is increased during file transfer.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> Default speed is 15 MHz; higher values may be used on faster systems.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Important:</strong> Too high values may cause performance issues on slower systems.
</p>


<h3>YMODEM Receive (yr) Packet Size</h3>

<p>
Press the <strong>VT Setup</strong> button (9).<br>
<strong>Result:</strong> The VT Setup window opens where Packet size can be set to Auto, 1024 or 128.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> Auto uses 1024 bytes when possible, and 128 bytes otherwise.
</p>

<p>
For details see the <a href="TerminalSetup.htm">Terminal Setup</a> section.
</p>

</body>
</html>
